  <iati-identifier>XM-DAC-7-PPR-250002732</iati-identifier>
  <reporting-org ref="XM-DAC-7" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ministry of Foreign Affairs of the Netherlands</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Confronting Sexual Corruption &amp; Abuse of Power affecting Vulnerable Groups including LGBTQI+ communities</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project aims to strengthen South Africa&#x2019;s response to sexual corruption by advocating for legal recognition, institutional accountability, and survivor protection, ensuring that women, girls, and LGBTQI+ persons can access justice without fear or discrimination.

This will be achieved through three complementary interventions:
1.Build the evidence &#x2013; assess how justice institutions handle sextortion cases, including training, prosecution, and referral systems.
2.Empower survivors and communities &#x2013; strengthen awareness, knowledge of rights, and safe reporting and support pathways.
3.Drive legal and policy reform &#x2013; use evidence and strategic advocacy to promote explicit legal recognition of sextortion and accountability within state institutions.

Expected Outcome
Practical, evidence-based understanding of how SAPS, the NPA, and other justice institutions address sextortion, with legal and procedural gaps identified and concrete recommendations developed to improve accountability.

Key Activities:
1.1. Research and document how SAPS and the NPA respond to sextortion, including institutional readiness, training, and practices.
1.2. Assess the NPA&#x2019;s capacity, challenges and willingness to prosecute sextortion-related cases under existing legislation.
1.3. Analyse reporting and referral mechanisms to understand barriers to justice, especially for women and LGBTQI+ survivors.
1.4. Capture case patterns and legal gaps through qualitative research.
1.5. Produce a research report and concise policy brief summarising findings and reform recommendations.
1.6. Host a national learning session or webinar to share findings with justice institutions, oversight bodies, and civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
